  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Enable cache keyed on package.json",
    "Explanation": [
      "No cache was restored in this run. The CircleCI config shows both restore_cache and save_cache steps are commented out (and their keys unset), so nothing could have been restored. The yarn log reports “No lockfile found.” — i.e. there is no yarn.lock in the checkout — so the only dependency manifest available for creating a checksum key is package.json. Yarn failed because the job runs yarn install --offline but the dependency cache was never restored, so offline install cannot find packages (left-pad). The single change that fixes this is to enable both restore_cache and save_cache and key them to a checksum of package.json (since yarn.lock is absent). This ensures the cache is saved after a successful run and restored on subsequent runs so yarn --offline can succeed. I did not choose dropping --offline because the job intends to use the local cache; enabling the cache is the minimal repair consistent with the pipeline's design. Also not chosen: checksum_yarn_lock, because yarn.lock is not present according to the log."
